<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croat–Serb Coalition</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1905–1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Croat–Serb Coalition was an alliance of Croatian and Serbian parties in Croatia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> formed in 1905, following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rijeka">Rijeka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zadar</a> resolutions. It promoted cooperation between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> against Hungarian and Austrian domination and held a majority in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-parliament">Croatian Sabor</a> from 1906 until 1918, when its leaders helped create the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-of-slovenes-croats-and-serbs">State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs</a>.</p></div>
